WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.770
There is a ground stop on our airport

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.540
and this thing is up in the sky.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:08.675
This thing

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.309
now believe

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.243
by the United States

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.345
to be a Chinese government spy balloon

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.248
flying 60,000 feet up in the atmosphere

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.449
over the country.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.751
We do know that the balloon

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.852
has violated U.S.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.987
airspace and international law,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.288
which is unacceptable.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:22.622
U.S.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.390
defense officials

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.524
have been tracking it closely

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.226
for several days, debating

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.660
whether to shoot it down

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.396
and advising President Joe Biden

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.797
it would be too dangerous.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.465
We assess that it does not pose

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:32.832
a risk

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.800
to people on the ground

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.602
as it currently is traversing

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.237
the continental United States.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.272
And so out of an abundance of caution,

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.608
Cognizant of the potential impact

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.443
to civilians on the ground

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.011
from a debris field.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.179
Right now, we're going to continue

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.181
to monitor and review options.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:48.982
The news breaking

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:49.682
just days

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.884
before Secretary of State

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.685
Antony Blinken was due to travel

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.553
to Beijing.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.421
The administration's

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.890
highest level trip to China so far.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:57.757
The trip now

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.794
postponed despite a rare Chinese apology

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.395
and claim that the balloon

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.997
was for civilian purposes

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.398
and floated off course.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.699
The presence of a surveillance

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.400
balloon in U.S.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.003
airspace is a clear violation of U.S.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.272
sovereignty and international law.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.808
That is an irresponsible act.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.076
And that the PRC's decision

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.444
to take this action

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.112
on the eve of my planned visit

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.280
is detrimental

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.481
to the substantive discussions

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.682
that we were prepared to have.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.850
The Pentagon says steps

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.517
have been taken

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.685
to protect sensitive

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.720
intelligence targets on the ground.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.256
The balloon is the size of three busses

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.492
equipped with solar panels for power

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.027
and a surveillance payload.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.062
Satellite and other data indicate

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.730
the balloon may have originated

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.798
in central China,

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:39.866
with weather patterns

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.567
pushing it out

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.635
over the Pacific Ocean into Canada

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.704
and down into the United States,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.439
where it has been crossing Montana

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.607
and into Missouri.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.175
It can maneuver itself

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.810
and has changed course.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.213
Currently floating over the central U.S.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.114
officials say,

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:54.814
while offering

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.850
little more on its precise location,

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.685
the public certainly has the ability

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.220
to look up in the sky and

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.387
and see where the balloon is.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.522
And they have

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.224
curiously training eyes

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.359
and cameras towards the skies.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.727
What planet is that

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.430
And, Jake, Secretary Blinken

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:10.864
has said

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.665
that he will reschedule his trip

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.168
to Beijing as soon as conditions allow.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.736
What those conditions are,

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.637
they will not say

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.271
but clearly

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.639
the temperature needs to come down.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.241
We just heard Secretary Blinken say now

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.408
the number one priority

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.643
is to get this balloon

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.378
out of our airspace.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.446
The Pentagon believes

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.780
that this could be several

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.948
more days, in fact.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.383
So they will keep watching it

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.317
as it floats on

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.786
by keeping their options open Jake.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.154
All right.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.288
Alex Marquardt at the U.S.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.122
State Department for us.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:36.689
Thank you so much.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.757
Let's bring in CNN

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.292
senior international correspondent

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.560
Ivan Watson in Hong Kong.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.661
CNN national security

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:42.462
correspondent Kylie

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.297
Atwood and CNN aviation

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.532
correspondent Pete Montaigne.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:45.832
And, Pete,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.333
I want to start with your brand

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:47.901
new reporting.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.701
You're learning

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.037
that pilots are reporting,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.873
seeing this balloon during their flights.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.041
Well, it is only a matter of time

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:55.742
before pilots

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:56.843
started spotting this, Jake.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.444
They're flying at high altitudes.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.612
And what's so interesting

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.447
is that they're reporting this balloon

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.317
only a few thousand feet above them.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.852
Look at this report

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.587
from the crew of a Cessna Citation.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:10.390
Private jet flying at 43,000 feet.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.191
They said

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:14.994
derelict balloon adrift at 50,000 feet.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.263
Only a 7000 foot difference there.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.398
They reported that

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.432
not all that long ago

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.900
near the Kansas City, Missouri

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.202
International Airport.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.003
What is also so interesting here

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.572
is that the Pentagon says

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:28.274
the balloon was cruising at 60,000 feet.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.175
So there's a question here

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.176
about whether or not

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.511
this balloon is descending.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.011
Remember,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.380
airliners are typically at an altitude

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.782
of about 30,000 feet.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.183
So the other big question here

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:37.984
is whether or not

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.452
this balloon will descend

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.387
and have more of an impact

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.623
on commercial air travel in the U.S..

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.791
We have already seen

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.926
that happen once before. On Wednesday.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.528
There was a ground stop

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.862
and flights were diverted

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.732
from about a 200 mile swath of airspace

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.101
between Helena and Billings, Montana.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.937
We know that lasted for 2 hours.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.138
Now, the question is

00:03:59.138 --> 00:03:59.672
whether or not

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.007
there will be more ground stops

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:01.741
because of this

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.942
and how this balloon

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.210
will descend to the ground.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.078
Will it pop

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.113
or will it come down gracefully?

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.648
Remember, what goes up comes

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.850
has to come down, Jake and Ivan.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.252
Secretary Blinken's trip

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.720
to China has been postponed.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.021
No future dates have been announced.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.322
We should note, it's

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.857
not often that a visit

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.058
to such a significant

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.526
adversary is made

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.894
by a secretary of state,

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:24.030
much less canceled.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.266
It seems like a fairly significant

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.467
diplomatic breach here.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:29.302
Absolutely.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:30.470
This is a big deal.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.206
And the relationship between the U.S.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:33.940
and China

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.942
have really soured

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.578
over the past couple of years.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.612
This trip

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:42.782
by Blinken was supposed to be building on

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.250
a meeting between

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.119
President Biden and the Chinese leader,

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.720
Xi Jinping, in Bali

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.922
at the G-20 summit in November.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.257
The Biden administration

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.091
had been complaining

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.226
that Chinese officials

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.628
simply weren't talking to U.S.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.462
officials

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.398
and there had been an agreement

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.533
to reopen lines of communication

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.069
and try to build guardrails to

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.170
to prevent the world's

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.672
two largest economies.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.040
The tensions from spiraling,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.474
spiraling out of control.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.143
So now you have this serious incident,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.211
which Blinken we just heard him

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.313
speaking from Korea,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.280
calling it

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.515
irresponsible,

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.550
a violation of international law,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.918
a violation of U.S.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.087
airspace and sovereignty,

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.689
but also saying, hey,

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.390
we've been able to communicate

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.059
directly about this

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:27.126
to prevent the tensions

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.362
from spiraling out of control.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.864
That seems to be paying some dividends

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:32.732
right now.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.634
At the same time, though,

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.502
the Biden administration has said

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.237
we cannot have this visit

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:38.971
at this time,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.174
that this is going to be a distraction

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.710
and there's a major problem here.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.612
So I do think we're seeing some results

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.715
of that diplomacy right now.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:49.549
The big question,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.150
what to do about this balloon,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.685
and I'm sure that U.S.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:53.753
security officials

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.121
would love to get their hands

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.489
on the technology

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.391
that the balloon is carrying right now.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.092
Yeah, indeed.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:05:59.492
And quite

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.694
clearly, the Pentagon confirmed today

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.563
this is not the first time

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.697
a surveillance balloon

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.865
has appeared over the United States,

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.200
but but previous instances

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.401
were not made public.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.702
So why is this time different

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.704
just because people in the public saw it?

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.873
I think that's part of it.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.975
I also think the fact that it happened

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:16.943
on the eve

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.378
of the secretary of state's planned

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.247
visit is also quite consequential here.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.648
We heard that from senior State

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.350
Department officials today saying,

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.419
yes, this has happened before,

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:28.254
but this is happening before this

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.122
major visit

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.923
that we had all been planning for.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.892
We don't think that visit can now be

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:34.293
as productive as we had hoped.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.528
That's why they're pulling it down.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:36.763
We heard just now

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:38.731
from the secretary of state saying that

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.032
the decision to take

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.034
this action is detrimental

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.569
on behalf of China.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.537
What that indicates

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:45.538
is that the United States

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.373
believes that it was deliberate,

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.142
that China actually allowed

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:49.976
or sent

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:52.111
this spy balloon over the United States,

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.513
perhaps it was even deliberate

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:55.114
that it happened right before this trip

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:55.948
was going to go ahead

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.817
sort of to test the United States.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.419
The other thing that he said

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.920
is that the United States right

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.088
now is focused

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.156
first and foremost

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:05.725
on getting this spy balloon out of U.S.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:06.259
airspace.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:07.960
What they're asking China to do.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.028
We really don't know.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.263
But he didn't count out

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.331
any additional repercussions

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.300
for China as a result of this,

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.368
you know, violating U.S.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.102
sovereignty

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.870
other than pulling down this trip Jake.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.338
And Ivan, on CNN earlier

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:21.140
today, the former secretary of defense

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.009
under Donald Trump Mark Esper, said

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:23.543
he finds it

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:24.911
curious that the Chinese government

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.913
is making excuses

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:27.947
instead of outright

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.116
denying that it's their balloon.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.984
What do you make of how Chinese officials

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:32.852
are handling this?

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.589
I'm really stunned, actually.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.024
I mean, I've been based here in Hong

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:39.859
Kong for more than seven years, Jake.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:42.028
I've never heard the Chinese government

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.563
expressing regret

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:46.299
over its actions before,

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.701
something akin to an apology right here,

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.570
basically coming out and saying,

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.805
yes, this is our balloon

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.373
and it's flown off course.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:55.208
They've they've

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:57.243
claimed that it is a meteorological

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.078
balloon,

00:07:59.078 --> 00:07:59.946
which, of course,

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.948
the Pentagon has challenged

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.483
that description of

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.785
of this of this thing.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:08.521
But it is a far cry from the tone

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:09.856
that we have typically heard

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:10.456
in past

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.258
years, this so-called wolf

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:14.026
warrior diplomacy

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:14.594
that's coming

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:15.661
out of the Chinese government

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:16.696
and Chinese officials

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:18.064
where they're aggressive

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:19.599
and nationalistic in

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:22.335
and pounce on things instead here.

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.003
There is acknowledgment

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.872
that this is theirs.

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:26.739
Maybe part of this

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.640
has to do with the fact

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.643
that Americans can see this thing with

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:33.679
the naked eye we just

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:36.916
the Chinese government is very opaque.

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:38.251
So it's hard to know

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.785
what could be the motivation

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.521
for sending this thing up in the air

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.656
at this time. Is it deliberate?

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:44.557
Is it, in fact,

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:45.157
an accident

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.426
that this thing blew off course?

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:50.329
But it is a huge symbol right now.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.532
And it's not just affecting the U.S..

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.934
China has summoned the.

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.336
Sorry, Canada has had to summon

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.171
the Chinese ambassador there

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.374
because it flew through Canadian airspace

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:02.275
as well.

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:05.077
So it does look embarrassing,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.213
I could argue, for the Chinese government

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:09.215
to have this giant thing floating around,

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.484
especially when China

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.052
makes such a big deal

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.720
about infringements

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.789
on its own national sovereignty

00:09:16.923 --> 00:09:18.758
and accuses the US of this

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:20.393
almost on a daily basis.

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:21.027
And Kylie,

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:22.728
you spoke to some family members

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:24.630
of one of the Americans currently

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.465
wrongfully detained in China,

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.734
and they were closely watching Secretary

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.303
Blinken's trip to Beijing

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:31.337
to see if their cases

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.872
were going to be brought up.

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:34.407
They must be very disappointed

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.775
in some ways.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:36.542
Of course,

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:38.578
this was an opportunity for them.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:39.512
They were really hoping

00:09:39.512 --> 00:09:40.580
that the secretary of State

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.314
was going to raise

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:43.015
all three Americans

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.750
who were wrongfully detained in China

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.419
in these meetings and potentially,

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:46.686
you know,

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:48.721
get some action on some back

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:50.690
and forth to try and get their release.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.024
But as we have seen

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.292
in US-China relations,

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:54.694
when there's one bad thing,

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.729
it often happens to have ripple effects

00:09:56.829 --> 00:09:57.863
on other efforts

00:09:57.863 --> 00:09:58.431
that they're trying

00:09:58.431 --> 00:09:59.432
to get going underway.

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:00.900
So this is not a good thing

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.001
for these families.

00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:02.702
Pete Montaigne,

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:03.636
Ivan Watson, Kylie

00:10:03.636 --> 00:10:04.670
Atwood, thanks so much. The.

